# THE PUBLIC-REPO ALLOWLIST (the owner, 2026-10-09: "i dont want to hide anything" — and the trading code never leaves).
#
# One git pathspec per line (a file, a directory, or a glob git understands). scripts/ops/publish-public-repo.sh copies exactly the
# TRACKED files these lines match into the public tree, at the same paths, and nothing else: ignored files (data/, .next/, builds,
# local env files) can never be matched because git does not track them. This is an allowlist, never a denylist — a new private
# directory is private by default; a new public file is published only when a line here names it.
#
# A line that matches no tracked file is reported as a warning (not an error), so a renamed directory is noticed.
# config/public-repo.denypatterns is the second gate: every copied text file is scanned against it, and the check fails on a hit.

# --- the on-chain program (Anchor) and its generator scripts ---
programs/burn-receipts

# --- the TypeScript client of the program ---
src/lib/burnReceipts
scripts/burnreceipts-*.mts

